```
=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: sshswitch
diagnosis_text:
The VLAN 6 inter-VLAN routing SVI on sshswitch is configured with the wrong
IP address. The device hosts VLAN gateway interfaces as Linux bridge SVIs:
br_v5 is correctly assigned 10.5.0.254/24 (serving PC1, PC2, dc_pc5 on
VLAN 5), but br_v6 — the SVI for VLAN 6 — is assigned 10.6.0.200/24
instead of the expected 10.6.0.254/24. Both PC3 (10.6.0.3/24) and PC4
(10.6.0.4/24) have their default gateway statically set to 10.6.0.254, an
address that does not exist anywhere in the network. Their ARP requests for
10.6.0.254 go unanswered, making the gateway completely unreachable. This
exclusively affects VLAN 6 because VLAN 5's br_v5 is correct; the L2
path itself is fully functional (PC3 can ping 10.6.0.200 with zero packet
loss, confirming switch4 → sshswitch VLAN 6 forwarding is intact). The
fault is localized to the sshswitch startup configuration where br_v6 is
given the IP 10.6.0.200/24 instead of 10.6.0.254/24.

Root cause: sshswitch's VLAN 6 SVI (br_v6) is misconfigured with IP
10.6.0.200/24 instead of the gateway address 10.6.0.254/24 that all VLAN 6
hosts expect.

Corrective fix: On sshswitch, remove the current IP from br_v6
(`ip addr del 10.6.0.200/24 dev br_v6`) and assign the correct gateway
address (`ip addr add 10.6.0.254/24 dev br_v6`). Persist the fix by
updating the corresponding line in sshswitch's startup configuration file
from 10.6.0.200/24 to 10.6.0.254/24.
=== END ===
```